\section{Environment variables}{

- `IMFEATURES_SKIP_PYTHON`: If `TRUE`, skip auto configuration on package load.
- `RETICULATE_PYTHON`: Absolute path to the Python binary reticulate should use.
- `IMFEATURES_METHOD`: One of `auto`, `conda`, `virtualenv`, `existing` to control
  `imfeatures_config()` behavior. On HPC, `virtualenv` or `existing` is recommended.
}

\section{Troubleshooting}{

- If you see a Conda error like "bad interpreter" while loading the package,
  you likely have a broken R-miniconda on the shared filesystem. Use the steps above
  or set `IMFEATURES_SKIP_PYTHON=TRUE` and call `use_existing_python()`.
- To avoid Conda entirely during configuration, set `IMFEATURES_METHOD=virtualenv`.
- `RETICULATE_PYTHON` is respected on load; set it to point at your Python
  to bypass any auto-detection.
}

